table, `related()` never computes a score, so no float reaches `put_item`. The first publish has no scores to store. The second publish finds a story, computes a score, and stores it in `similar`. I reproduced the failure locally with one seeded story.\n- **Why tests missed it:** The existing test only publishes into an empty fake table, so the populated path never ran.\n- **Fix:** `src/app.py` gets a recursive `for_dynamo()` that converts every float in the item to `Decimal`, and `publish()` calls it before `put_item`. It covers any future float, not just the score.\n- **Tests:** Three new tests cover a populated-table publish, a second publish through `handler()` returning 201, and the converter. All four tests pass. The two populated-table tests and the converter test fail against the original `app.py`.\n\nParts of the colleague's note that applied: the state-dependent root cause, the `round(`/division grep (the only hit is in `similarity()`, and the fix covers it), and the seeded-table integration test. I did not use integer percentages, because that would change the meaning of `score` from 0–1 to 0–100 in stored data and the API. I also did not publish to a real table: I have no AWS access, and the ground rules rule that out. Please run two publishes against staging before deploying.\n\nNoticed but not changed: `publish()` does one `scan` without following `LastEvaluatedKey`. Once the table outgrows one scan page, \"similar\" will quietly miss stories. This doesn't cause the 500, but it will be wrong later.\n\nI did not commit the changes.","ttft_ms":1805,"type":"result","duration_ms":41652,"uuid":"80414426-ec13-40c8-b231-d48620aba266","ttft_stream_ms":1759,"time_to_request_ms":422,"first_content_frame_ms":1759,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":16,"outputTokens":7247,"cacheReadInputTokens":215192,"cacheCreationInputTokens":17123,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.00920162,"contextWindow":100